## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA workflow for data privacy policy failures, including evidence capture and cross-tenant rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling for evidence and artifacts
- Lifecycle state machine and ownership
- Minimal REST API design with linked logs/traces
- Tenant/region metrics for containment and recurrence
- RCA templates and canary rollout planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// CAPA core types (overview)
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidence: string[];
  artifacts: string[];
  state: 'detected'|'triaged'|'in_progress'|'contained'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
  links?: { type: string; url: string }[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale CAPA data stores across regions?
- How to ensure regulatory auditability and evidence integrity?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical CAPA design for data segregation issues in multi-tenant exports, focusing on traceability and measurable containment.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API design
- Metrics to prove effectiveness
- RCA templates and canary-based remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
let caps = [];
app.post('/caps', (req,res)=>{ const cap = req.body; cap.id = cap.id || String(Date.now()); caps.push(cap); res.status(201).json(cap);});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you store and attach evidence files?
- How would you enforce tenant isolation in the API and data store?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design for policy drift in cross-tenant data sharing, integrating data contracts, policy-as-code, region controls, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, policy_version, contract_id, tenant_id, region.
- Policy-as-code and a central contract registry.
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine.
- Minimal REST API for CAPAs linked to logs/traces.
- Metrics: recurrence_rate, MTTR, false_positive_rate by region/tenant; RCA template; canary rollout.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal REST endpoint sketch for creating a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  // validate body, persist CAPA, attach logs/traces
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate policy drift across regions automatically after a contract update?
- What telemetry would you add to detect cross-tenant leakage events in near real-time?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical CAPA design skills: data modeling, lifecycle governance, lightweight APIs, and measurable containment strategies in a multi-tenant, multi-region setup.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model tailored to tenants/regions
- Lifecycle state machine with auditable transitions
- Minimal REST API for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region/tenant-aware metrics to prove containment
- RCA template and canary remediation plan

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  tenants: string[];
  regions: string[];
  evidence: string[];
  batchInfo: {
    schedule: string;
    duration: number;
    resources: string[];
  };
  rootCause: string;
  corrective: string;
  preventive: string;
  owner: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
};

// Lifecycle states
type CAPAState = 'Identified' | 'Contained' | 'Investigating' | 'Corrected' | 'Verified';

// REST API endpoints
POST /capas
PUT /capas/:id
GET /capas?tenant=:t&region=:r&state=:s
```

## Metrics & Containment
- Tenant/region latency percentiles pre/post containment
- Batch job resource utilization by tenant/region
- Error rates and success rates during remediation
- Canary deployment success metrics by region

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical CAPA program around data privacy, tenant isolation, and controlled policy changes in real-time fintech systems.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model: evidence, lineage, owners, policy references
- Tenant-aware lifecycle: detect, contain, remediate, verify with SLAs
- Minimal API: create/update CAPAs with logs/traces, policy links
- Metrics: containment time, recurrence rate, tenant impact
- RCA and canary rollback: structured **root cause** templates and safe rollout controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sketch: POST /api/capa
app.post('/api/capa', (req, res) => {
  const {evidence, lineage, owners, policyLink, tenantId} = req.body;
  // validate inputs, create CAPA, emit logs, assign owners
  res.status(201).json({capaId: 'CAPA-1234'});
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce tenant isolation in evidence and logs metadata?
- What would be your go/no-go criteria for canary rollback validation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the candidate's ability to define a data-driven CAPA program for supply-chain vulnerabilities in multi-region systems, balancing traceability, regional scoping, and automated rollout.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data modeling with SBOM, CVEs, tenants, regions
- Region-aware lifecycle state machines
- Minimal REST API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces
- Metrics for containment, recurrence, MTTR
- RCA templates and canary rollout controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal TypeScript types for CAPA
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenants: string[];
  region: string;
  cveId: string;
  sbom: string;
  logs: string[];
  containment: string;
  correctiveAction: string;
  preventiveAction: string;
  rca: string;
  status: 'detected'|'triaged'|'contained'|'eradicated'|'verified'|'closed';
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model time-to-containment vs time-to-eradication in your metrics?
- What governance ensures SBOM accuracy across auto-updates?
